PineForge Pine v6 documentation
================================

Source:  https://github.com/fullpass-4pass/pineforge-engine, paths
         docs/pine_v6_audit_master.md
         docs/pages/*.md
License: Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory)

`pine_v6_audit_master.md` is PineForge contributors' standalone audit of
Pine v6: 38 critical + ~62 minor known divergences between TradingView's
published reference and the actual codegen/runtime behaviour.

`pages/*.md` (18 files) are PineForge's narrative explainers covering
Pine v6 concepts in depth: magnifier, mtf, timeframes, lifecycle,
report-schema, abi-stability, configuration, integration / ffi / examples,
tutorials. Together they're the "how does X work" prose reference for
Pine v6 + the PineForge runtime.

Local modifications:
  - Em-dash (U+2014), en-dash (U+2013), and NBSP (U+00A0) characters
    (26 in the audit, 149 across the 18 pages) were rewritten to their
    ASCII equivalents so the files pass pine-oracle's gremlin scan. The
    rewrite is punctuation/whitespace-only and does not change rendered
    semantics; see commit history for the exact changes.

pine-oracle indexes the audit at build time via `src/search.rs` exposing
its sections as `kind: "audit"` results, and indexes the narrative pages
as `kind: "docs"` results. The upstream files remain the canonical source;
consumers seeing a hit should expand the section title through the section
structure documented in the upstream file.

Snapshot date: see git log for the introducing commits.
